## 🔬 Exhaustive Permutations Matrix Across All Subsystems

### 1. Treatment Type & Indication Permutations

| Treatment Type | Specific Clinical Parameters | Tooth Selection & Chart Behavior | 3D & Imaging Workflow |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Single Crown / Inlay / Onlay / Veneer** | Occlusal clearance (0.5mm–2.0mm), Margin type (Chamfer, Shoulder, Feather), Contact design (Normal, Tight, Light). | Single tooth selected on FDI chart. Color code: Blue (Crown), Pink (Veneer), Cyan (Inlay). | Upper/Lower STL scan + buccal bite registration. Spatial margin spline inspection. |
| **Multi-Unit Bridge (e.g. 3–4 Units)** | Connector design (Anatomical, Oval, Reduced), Pontic design (Ovate, Sanitary, Modified Ridge Lap). | Contiguous teeth selection (max 6 per jaw). Bridge connector lines rendered between abutments & pontics. | Path-of-insertion check & undercut evaluation. |
| **Surgical Implant & Custom Abutment** | Implant Brand (Nobel Biocare, Straumann, Osstem, Dentium), Scan Body Model, Analog Logistics (`Clinic Provided` vs `Lab Provided`), Abutment Type (Screw-retained vs Ti-Base Hybrid). | Implant screw chimney icon rendered over tooth root on FDI chart. | IOS scan body STL + Optional CBCT DICOM volume with nerve canal mapping. |
| **Removable Denture / Nightguard** | Material (Dual-Laminate Acrylic, Cast Framework, Valplast, 3D Resin), Arch (Upper/Lower/Dual). | Full arch selection or edentulous ridge mapping. | Dual-arch STL impression + tissue relief clearance parameters. |

---

### 2. Clinical Encounter $\leftrightarrow$ Lab Case Living Synchronization

| Operational Trigger | Patient EHR & Odontogram Effect | Lab Production Effect |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Case Submitted for Production (Tooth #14)** | Tooth #14 on 32-tooth odontogram automatically turns **Striped Blue / Yellow** ("Under Fabrication"). | Lab receives new ticket in `Pending` queue with 5-tab prescription specs. |
| **Lab Advances Status to `DISPATCHED`** | Patient record displays green transit badge; 1-click WhatsApp notification available to alert patient. | Case milestone event added to bi-temporal ledger. |
| **Dentist Marks Case `FITTED / COMPLETED`** | Tooth #14 permanently transitions to **Solid Green/Blue ("Existing Zirconia Crown")** in patient's master record. | Case archived with permanent CAD soft-copy and warranty ID. |
| **Try-In Failed / Remake Requested** | Clinician clicks `[Request Remake]` directly on the tooth; previous record preserved in Merkle ledger; new iteration linked. | Lab receives remake ticket with attached clinical adjustment notes and discrepancy photos. |
| **Ambient Voice Dictation Encounter** | Voice engine records SOAP notes, 6-point perio probing, and pre-fills the 5-tab lab prescription modal. | Instant 1-click case submission from the encounter. |

